instr:
Cog cannot round-trip executable files, empty directories, and relative symbolic links through managed-weight discovery, packing, OCI transport, pulling, and reconstruction. Add reproducible filesystem metadata without weakening containment or changing ordinary regular-file workflows.

FileSource, HTTPSource, and HFSource inventories must publish normalized regular, directory, or symbolic-link metadata as identity after rejecting unstable, unsupported, or escaping entries. HTTP defaults to one non-executable regular file. Executable policy changes only its permission; directory and symbolic-link policies fail before download. Serialize typed lock entries in canonical normalized-path order with byte-identical repeated output. Metadata-aware identity must reflect semantic changes even when bytes do not. OCI metadata, archives, locks, and reconstructed trees must agree on path, kind, portable mode, link target, and set identity.

Before reconstruction, validate unique archive headers and complete link chains against metadata and containment. Create entries in dependency order with recorded portable permissions. Publish atomically, reporting collisions without replacing unrelated destination entries. Legacy locks and configurations without metadata remain regular files with prior serialization and archive behavior. EntryMetadata has fields Kind EntryKind, Mode uint32, LinkTarget string and serializes under the JSON key "metadata" with nested keys "kind", "mode", and "linkTarget";
